  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the sarcastic meme format and its textual content",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the meme's structure and text, which uses the phrase 'in case you missed the debate...' to imply the user is the one who 'missed' the debate, thereby positioning the user as the audience being addressed. The escalating text ('free stuff!', 'more free stuff!', 'even more free stuff!') is also projected onto the user as the recipient of this sarcastic commentary, creating a sense of being targeted or mocked for not being aware of the 'free stuff' focus. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'your', but the framing device 'in case you missed the debate...' creates an implicit projection onto the user as the intended audience.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
